<Base title="About"><section class="shell editorial"><span class="eyebrow">ABOUT SIMUBOX</span><h1>An open laboratory for scientific ideas.</h1><p class="lead">SimuBox connects interactive experiments to the models, assumptions, references and source code behind them.</p><h2>How it works</h2><p>Browse the catalogue by scientific field. Play first-party experiments in the browser and change their parameters. Read the accompanying explanation to understand what the model says and where it stops. External candidate projects are listed for discovery and attribution while integration remains under review.</p><h2>What comes next</h2><p>The platform is an early working foundation. We plan to investigate secure manual integration of independently maintained browser simulations. Accounts, uploads and automatic execution of third-party code are outside this release.</p><h2>Origins</h2><p>Yahya (<a href="https://github.com/yahyabmo">yahyabmo</a>) contributed the initial conceptual research that informed SimuBox. The comparison with existing platforms remains a product hypothesis, not a verified market claim.</p></section></Base>
